Hi everyone,

I have a workstation equipped with 8x L20 GPUs and 2TB of RAM.

I am trying to run the GLM-5.2 Q4 quantized model using `ik_llama.cpp`. I compiled the source code using g++ 11.4 and CUDA 13.0. However, when running the model, I am getting random characters and gibberish output.

To troubleshoot, I pulled the latest upstream `llama.cpp` source code and compiled it in the exact same environment. Interestingly, llama.cpp works perfectly and produces normal output, though it feels a bit slow.

I have attached my launch command and the actual output logs below. Any help or insights would be greatly appreciated. Thank you so much!

The test command is very simple:
```
curl http://localhost:8080/v1/chat/completions -H "Content-Type: application/json" -d '{"messages":[{"role": "user", "content": "请简单介绍一下你自己。"}], "stream": true}'
```
("请简单介绍一下你自己。" is Chinese, which means "Please introduce yourself simply.")

script for ik_llama.cpp:
```sh
